# Dual-use disclosure

Package: @socketsecurity/bun-security-scanner
Content policy class: dual-use (https://docs.npmjs.com/policies/dual-use)

## Dual-use functionality

This package is a security research utility. It registers as Bun's
`install.security` scanner, hooks the package-manager install flow, inspects
package metadata and contents while an install is in progress, queries Socket
threat-intelligence advisories over the network, and blocks or warns on
packages that match known-malicious or policy-violating signatures. Install
hooking, mid-install package inspection, and advisory lookups are behaviors
that can resemble malicious software to automated scanning.

## Intended legitimate use

Defensive supply-chain protection for developers using the Bun package
manager: stopping known-malicious, hijacked, or policy-violating dependencies
before they are installed. The package provides no exploitation, persistence,
exfiltration, or obfuscation capability, collects no credentials, and sends
only package identifiers needed for advisory lookups. Source and issue
tracker: https://github.com/SocketDev/bun-security-scanner
